      "message": "docs: post-processor scripts are exempt from the 400-line law\n\nA .cps post script is one file the post engine loads and runs for one\nmachine dialect; it stays whole at whatever length the dialect needs\n(user, 2026-11-08: \"CPS files cannot follow the 400 line rules as its a\nscript to be executed by a post processor, and it needs what it needs\").\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
